      "description": "Bordered tonal surface used for pause and result states over the app scrim.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h2>Take a breath.</h2><p>Your flight is right where you left it.</p><button class=\"ds-primary\">Resume flight</button><button class=\"ds-secondary\">Choose another world</button></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:Manrope,sans-serif;width:min(380px,100%);padding:30px;text-align:center;background:var(--surface,#131e24);color:var(--ink,#f3f3dc);border:1px solid var(--line,#afc2bc38);border-radius:12px;box-shadow:0 22px 70px #00000066}.ds-panel h2{font-family:Chakra,sans-serif;font-size:32px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.03em;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 12px}.ds-panel>p{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted,#b4c1bc);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 23px}.ds-panel .ds-primary{width:100%}.ds-primary{font-family:Manrope,sans-serif;background:var(--accent,#e9edaa);color:var(--on-accent,#172020);border:1px solid var(--accent,#e9edaa);border-radius:6px;min-height:54px;padding:15px 21px;font-size:15px;font-weight:800;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:18px;cursor:pointer;transition:background .2s,transform .2s var(--ease,cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)),box-shadow .2s;box-shadow:0 7px 22px #00000029}.ds-primary:hover{background:var(--ink,#f3f3dc);transform:translateY(-2px);box-shadow:0 9px 24px #00000040}.ds-primary:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-primary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent,#e9edaa);outline-offset:5px}.ds-primary:disabled{opacity:.55;cursor:wait}.ds-primary svg{width:21px;height:21px;fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.6;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}.ds-secondary{font-family:Manrope,sans-serif;background:transparent;color:var(--ink,#f3f3dc);border:1px solid var(--line,#afc2bc38);border-radius:6px;min-height:48px;padding:12px 20px;font-size:12px;font-weight:650;display:block;width:100%;margin-top:12px;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s}.ds-secondary:hover{background:#e5e2ce0a}.ds-secondary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent,#e9edaa);outline-offset:5px}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation-duration:.001ms!important;transition-duration:.001ms!important}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Small wings, immense worlds",
    "overview": "A small, determined bird sits against immense procedural landscapes. Lunar silver and acid ivory establish the quiet baseline; blood rose and lava amber shift the same controls into Nightmare and Hell. Fine contours, soft atmospheric gradients, and tangible buttons keep the scenes illustrated while controls stay precise.\n\nThe playfield fills the viewport. The menu gives way to edge information during flight, and a compact centered panel handles pause and results. The interface uses original Canvas creatures and inline SVG contours rather than an image-heavy component shell.\n\nDeath counts sit alongside personal records: the menu footer shows selected-world deaths and the all-world total, the bottom flight HUD shows DEATHS, and results use four stat columns including Deaths. Each actual crash increments its world count once; pausing, leaving a run, and preparing a retry do not.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Three mode-bound palettes on one shared control system.",
      "Full-viewport scenery with compact edge information.",
      "Chakra numerals and display; Manrope instructions and controls.",
      "Dashed warnings become solid active hazards."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The World Binding Rule",
        "body": "Changing worlds updates accent, on-accent, muted text, surface, divider, and deep background together; ink stays shared.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Warning Grammar Rule",
        "body": "Keep warning sightlines dashed and active beams solid. Wrath warnings and beams span the visible playfield even while the emitter is offscreen.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Split Rule",
        "body": "Use compact labels for live status and records; use the reading role for the flight guide. Preserve the larger help-text overrides when changing responsive styles.",
        "section": "typography"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do bind controls to the active world through the existing CSS custom properties.",
      "Do preserve full-height scaling and safe-area offsets when changing the viewport layout.",
      "Do keep explicit warning geometry, focus outlines, and reduced-motion behavior alongside visual changes."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace the three world identities with difficulty labels.",
      "Don't stretch the Canvas to a fixed portrait arena or crop away the extra world visible on wide screens.",
      "Don't shrink guide paragraphs to compact HUD-label sizes."
    ]
  }
}
